#!build/cubical
-- lib/chat.cub — a reply to a turn, computed from the record (docs/language-derived-from-the-record.cub):
-- the turn's words select their past occurrences in the record, each word weighted by how few
-- occurrences it has (a rare word identifies, a word everywhere identifies nothing); the sentence where
-- the selected occurrences meet most heavily, and the sentence that followed it, are the reply: what
-- followed the selected past occurrences, carried to now. The record is the store's prose, every
-- comment of the code and every document, cut into sentences once into build/chat/record; each turn
-- and its reply are appended to it, so the conversation is record too and later turns select from it.
-- No weights, no training: the record is read as it is.
--   hyperactive chat TEXT        the reply to TEXT
--   echo TEXT | hyperactive chat
--   hyperactive chat --reset     the conversation forgotten (the record made again from the store)
import "host.cub"

